## API Reference

### SankeyChart Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|------|
| `nodes` | `SankeyNodeData[]` | — | `{ name, color?, value?, tooltipData?, isDrillable?, childCount? }`. |
| `links` | `SankeyLinkData[]` | — | `{ source, target, value, isDrillable? }`, index references. |
| `height` | `number` | `400` | Pixel height. |
| `width` | `number` | measured | Explicit width (SSR/tests). |
| `nodeWidth` | `number` | `8` | Node bar width. |
| `nodePadding` | `number` | `10` | Vertical gap between nodes in a column. |
| `showNodeValues` | `boolean \| 'auto'` | `'auto'` | `'auto'` enables labels when any node has a `value`. |
| `nodeLabelLayout` | `'stacked' \| 'inline'` | `'stacked'` | Value above the name / on one line. |
| `formatValue` | `(v: number) => string` | `toLocaleString` | Value formatter. |
| `showTooltip` | `boolean` | `true` | Hover tooltip. |
| `defaultNodeColor` | `string` | — | Fallback before the categorical palette. |
| `left` / `right` | `number \| string` | `'5%'` | Layout insets (px or percent). |
| `linkColor` | `'gradient' \| 'gray'` | `'gradient'` | Link fill mode. |
| `linkOpacity` | `number` | `0.5` | Gradient link opacity. |
| `labels` | `Partial<SankeyLabels>` | English | `{ instructions }`: read after each node's name. |

### SankeyChart Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `node-click` | `(node: SankeyNodeData)` | Node clicked; the original datum. |
| `link-click` | `(link: SankeyLinkData)` | Link clicked; the original datum. |

### SankeyChart Slots

| Slot | Scope | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `tooltip` | `{ params: SankeyTooltipParams }` | Replaces the tooltip body; `params.type` is `'node' \| 'link'`. |

## Node Dragging

Nodes move vertically. Each stays in its column and its links re-route live.

| Input | Effect |
|------|------|
| Drag a node | Follows the pointer 1:1 from where it was grabbed, inside the chart's height. Past 4 px the press never fires `node-click`. |
| Release | The node stays where it was dropped. |
| `Escape` during a drag | Cancels; the node springs back to where it was picked up. |
| Double-click the background | Springs every node back to the computed layout. |
| `Alt` + `↑` / `↓` on a focused node | Moves it 8 px. |
| `Enter` / `Space` on a focused node | Selects it (`node-click`). |

Nodes take focus (`role="button"`, named by the node) and read `labels.instructions` after the name; it merges over `SANKEY_DEFAULT_LABELS`. A touch drag that starts on a node moves it instead of scrolling the page; a touch on a link or the background still scrolls. Different `nodes` (names, values), `links` (ends, values) or `height` start over from the computed layout and drop every move; a new array with the same content keeps them. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` the springs jump to their end state; a dragged node still follows the pointer.

## Resilience

Circular links make d3-sankey throw — the component catches that, renders an empty state and logs a dev warning instead of crashing the host page.

## Hover Highlight

Hovering a node or a link leaves only adjacent elements untouched: the non-adjacent nodes, links and labels dim together to 10% opacity, matching ECharts' `emphasis.focus: 'adjacency'` (blur is `fromState.opacity * 0.1`), switched on the frame the pointer arrives rather than over ECharts' 300ms `cubicOut` (TuffEx's hover rule). A node's neighbourhood is itself, every link touching it and the nodes at those links' other ends; a link's is itself, its two endpoint nodes and every link touching either endpoint.

Sankey has **no geometry animation** when the data changes, which is parity with kumo rather than a missing feature: ECharts' `SankeyView` has neither `initProps` nor `updateProps`, so when the d3-sankey layout changes the nodes and links land on their new positions without a tween. Only the drag's own springs (Escape, reset) move. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` the 300ms transition drops out and the highlight switches instantly.

## Differences from kumo

- `tooltipFormatter` (HTML strings + manual XSS escaping) → the `tooltip` slot (VNodes).
- kumo's nodes are fixed; here a node can be dragged, nudged with `Alt` + arrow keys and reset.
- kumo throws on circular input; this degrades to an empty render with a dev warning.
